    "body": "---\nname: \"system-check\"\ndescription: \"/system-check - Full System Status\"\nversion: \"1.0.0\"\nauthor: \"burp-ai (ported)\"\ntags: [\"pentest\", \"utility\", \"system-check\"]\ntrigger_patterns:\n  - \"/system-check\"\n  - \"check pentest tools\"\n  - \"verify system setup\"\n---\n\n# /system-check - Full System Status\n\n**This is NOT the Burp status tool. Do NOT call Burp's status tool.**\n\nWhen user types `/system-check`, you must execute ALL actions below IN ORDER.\n\n---\n\n## ACTION 1: List All Agents\n\nRun this bash command and capture output:\n```bash\nfor f in the equivalent Void tool do basename \"$f\" .md; done\n```\n\n## ACTION 2: List All Skills\n\nRun this bash command and capture output:\n```bash\nfor f in the equivalent Void tool do basename \"$f\" .md; done\n```\n\n## ACTION 3: List MCP Servers\n\nRead the file the equivalent Void tool and extract all server names from the `mcpServers` object.\n\n## ACTION 4: Test Burp Connection\n\nCall the Burp MCP `status` tool to verify connectivity.\n\n## ACTION 5: List Pentests\n\nRun: `ls the equivalent Void tool to show existing pentests.\n\n---\n\n## OUTPUT FORMAT\n\nAfter completing ALL actions above, display results in this format:\n\n```\n==========================================\n  BURP AI AGENT - SYSTEM CHECK\n==========================================\n\nAGENTS FOUND:\n   - orchestrator\n   - pentester\n   - auditor\n   - bughunter\n\nSKILLS FOUND:\n   - /basic-recon\n   - /xss\n   - /obfuscate\n   - /poc\n   - /repeater\n   - /pentest-help\n   - /system-check\n\nMCP SERVERS:\n   - burpsuite-mcp (sse)\n   - playwright (stdio)\n   - filesystem (stdio)\n\nBURP CONNECTION:\n   [Result from Burp status tool]\n\nPENTESTS:\n   [List of domains or \"No pentests yet\"]\n\n==========================================\n```\n\n---\n\n## CHECKLIST\n\nBefore displaying output, confirm you have:\n- [ ] Ran bash command to list agents\n- [ ] Ran bash command to list skills\n- [ ] Read settings.json for MCP servers\n- [ ] Called Burp status tool\n- [ ] Listed pentests directory\n\nDO NOT skip any step. The user expects to see agents, skills, AND MCPs.\n\n## Tooling note\n\nThis methodology came from a container-based agent. In Void you drive it with the panel tools instead: `send_request` for individual probes, `run_intruder_attack` for payload sweeps, `run_hybrid_scan` for the deterministic checks, `compare_responses` for baseline diffing, and `add_pentest_finding` to record a confirmed result. There is no shell and no filesystem — do not attempt to run scripts."
